h(S,'S2. Contact definitions and full stage counts')
p(S,'PDB ATOM/HETATM coordinates are parsed as Å into float64 arrays. Hydrogen and deuterium atoms are excluded. Atoms are identified by chain, residue number, insertion code, residue name and atom name, with duplicate identities or nonfinite coordinates rejected. For this fixed single-chain, consecutively numbered 1-63 system, nonadjacent means absolute residue-number separation greater than one. Same-residue/adjacent-residue pairs are omitted; each remaining unordered atom pair is counted once. Distances are Euclidean without periodic wrapping. A contact requires d < 1.6 Å; equality is noncontact.')
p(S,'General stage prevalence counts frames with any eligible contact. The union counts frames with any contact in any stage. Let C_s be the set of exact unordered atom-pair identities present at stage s. Strict recontact requires a pair p with p in C_i, p absent from C_j, and p in C_k for i < j < k. Persistence alone is insufficient. PHE6-PHE55 recontact uses the binary residue-pair sequence b_s and an ordered 1-0-1 triple; the minimum-pair atom names may differ. This distinction is explicit in code/verify_e1_from_pdb.py.')
