p(S,'The historical runs used Python 3.13.1, OpenMM 8.2.0, MDTraj 1.11.2 and NumPy 2.5.4. The fixed BioEmu source adds a C-terminal OXT, then hydrogens and solvent. AMBER99SB (amber99sb.xml) and TIP3P (tip3p.xml), 1.0-nm padding, 0.1 M NaCl, PME with 1.0-nm cutoff, hydrogen-bond constraints and rigid water were used. Each input has 494 protein heavy atoms; the returned final protein structure has 495 including OXT. The contact criterion excludes adjacent/same-residue terms, and all four final structures have zero qualifying pairs.')
h(S,'S5.2. Integrator, restraints and actual platform',2)
p(S,'After setting coordinates/thermal velocities and applying constraints (1e-7), minimizeEnergy was called with source-default settings. Langevin integration at 300 K used initial friction 200 ps⁻¹ and constraint tolerance 1e-5. Four stabilization blocks of 0.1 ps each used timesteps 1e-6, 1e-5, 1e-4 and 1e-3 ps: 100,000 + 10,000 + 1,000 + 100 steps. NVT then used 100,000 steps at 0.001 ps and friction 10 ps⁻¹ (0.1 ns). NPT used 400,000 steps, friction 1 ps⁻¹ and a 1-bar MonteCarloBarostat (0.4 ns). Total: 611,100 steps and 0.5004 ns. No free-production phase was executed (simtime_ns=0).')
p(S,'The positional potential is k × periodicdistance² with numerical k=1000 in OpenMM’s kJ/mol and nm unit convention, not a silently substituted ½kx² parameterization. It remains active throughout. The code selects atom names N, CA, C and O across the whole system; water oxygens named O can therefore also be restrained. These records must not be called unrestrained or protein-backbone-only free MD. Actual saved platform properties are OpenCL / single precision on Intel Iris Xe Graphics, irrespective of the original CPU-oriented task plan. Stepping probes split calls into chunks ≤1,000 and add synchronization; the stochastic path can differ from an uninstrumented invocation.')
