h(S,'S6. Protein heavy-atom LJ proxy')
h(S,'S6.1. Pair set and parameters',2)
p(S,'Stage A evaluates the common 494 original protein heavy atoms, with 116,140 eligible nonadjacent interresidue pairs per structure (464,560 pair rows total). Same-residue and adjacent-residue pairs and zero-epsilon exclusions are omitted. AMBER99SB nonbonded parameters come from the historical protein-only NoCutoff surrogate; Lorentz-Berthelot mixing uses arithmetic σ and geometric ε. Original NonbondedForce exception parameters are honored where applicable. Temporary OXT and added hydrogens enable force-field typing only and are excluded from the analyzed 494-heavy-atom pair set.')
p(S,'Each pair contributes 4ε[(σ/r)¹²-(σ/r)⁶], with r and σ in nm, ε and energy in kJ/mol. No solvent, ion, electrostatic, bonded, hydrogen-containing-pair or whole-system term is included. The historical Phase1A audit independently checked parameter typing (952 particles and 5,144 exceptions in the typing systems); P1 retained that evidence but did not repeat system construction or hydrogen optimization. P1 recalculated pairwise arithmetic from the archived σ/ε values and measured every analyzed pair distance from the original PDBs.')
fig(S,'Figure_S2','Figure S2. Positive archived net protein heavy-atom LJ proxy values for the two selected original/locally perturbed pairs, on a logarithmic y axis. Connecting lines identify paired selected structures, not a thermodynamic path. Values use archived Stage A summaries; Table S4 separates coordinate precision and CSV-summation variants.')
